sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch13-16> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch13-16--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch13-16--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on darwin1859-ch13-16: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.57" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.575"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.6"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Embryo-versus-adult distance is a clear criterion, and public expression archives plus specimen imagery can support it for small sets of vertebrates. That is a restricted scope relative to animals within a class. The comparison can discriminate the claim from ecology-driven embryonic resemblance, but assembling comparable stages across more than a handful of species is slow specialist work." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Within classes, compare multivariate morphological or transcriptomic distances among species at matched embryonic stages and at adult stages, and test whether embryonic similarity is independent of habitat similarity. The claim is confirmed if embryos of a class cluster more tightly than adults and embryonic closeness does not track shared conditions, and refuted if adults are as similar as embryos or embryonic resemblance follows ecology." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Matched embryonic stages exist mainly for model vertebrates and a few insects, not for animals of a whole class.", "Staging landmarks are not equivalent across phyla, so an 'early' stage in one group is not the same comparison in another.", "Transcriptome studies often find a mid-development hourglass rather than uniform embryonic similarity, which the morphometric data must be allowed to show." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch13-16--grok--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch13-16--grok--dataset-2>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch13-16--grok--dataset-3> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch13-16--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of darwin1859-ch13-16 by Grok 4.7: 0.75" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.75"^^xsd:double ;
